CORE
main.c
--unwind 5 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Companion of `symbolic_malloc_per_thread_index`: same symbolic-size `malloc`
region, but both threads write the same constant index, a genuine race. It
must stay FAILED before and after the fix, confirming that suppressing the
framed sentinel offset for this family does not suppress a real collision.
